					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: PING-PONG COLORS\n\nIn this example we use the Expand node in ping-pong mode to expand a Linear node set to produce colors.\nThe Linear produces only two colors, but the Expand node will increase the size of the collection equal to the Size slider(which is a Int In node).\n\nAs the Size increases and decreases the amount of colors is adjusted accordingly, maintaining the ping-pong effect. \n\nHave a play with the different wrapping modes on the Expand node and notice the difference."
					}
				},
